{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e","id":1377395,"title":"By The Pricking of My Thumbs \u2013 John Doe\u2019s Guide to Demon Summoning (3E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-30T14:42:20-07:00","id":1377395,"title":"By The Pricking of My Thumbs \u2013 John Doe\u2019s Guide to Demon Summoning (3E)","content":"<u><b>Introduction</b></u><br /> <br /> Recently I saw a post about someone struggling with summoned demons and thought there\u2019s scope for my to provide a mini-guide.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been playing RPGs for nearly three decades, have a strong mathematical background and came to RPGs from strategy games. I\u2019ve been a big Exalted fan since the game first came out. Third Edition is significantly different to previous editions, and this is decidedly a Third Edition guide \u2013 some of it is based on my Second Edition experience, but this guide is definitively not intended to be for Second Ed.<br /> <br /> Because I\u2019m old, I still see the need to put these disclaimers in: Exalted is a game of <i>fantasy. </i>You cannot really summon demons to do your bidding. Exalted\u2019s demons <i>do not exist</i>. This guide will not help you summon demons in real life, and even if it did, you <i>shouldn\u2019t </i>summon demons in real life. In Exalted, you can pretend to solve world hunger. It doesn\u2019t actually solve world hunger. You can pretend to summon demons. You\u2019re not actually summoning demons. Some games let you pretend to be a championship football manager. Some games let you pretend to be a Native American fighting invaders. Exalted lets you pretend to summon demons.<br /> <br /> <u><b>What\u2019s a demon anyway?</b></u><br /> <br /> From \u201c\u03b4\u03b1\u03af\u03bc\u03c9\u03bd\u201d meaning \u201cspirit\u201d or \u201cdivine power\u201d, the word \u201cdemon\u201d is inexorably linked to Christian Apocrypha, which describes demons as evil beings in thrall to Satan (the very personification of evil and adversary to god).<br /> <br /> Exalted, which has spirits, gods, elemental beings and fae creatures. Exalted\u2019s demons are not named coincidentally.<br /> <br /> Whilst Exalted\u2019s demons have little in common with the demons of Christian Pop Culture, they <i>are </i>invisible, intangible beings, cast out from the world to a prison of eternal torment.<br /> <br /> Demons descend from the <i>Yozi</i>: ancient enemies of the gods, cast down and imprisoned within the body of their King, <i>Malfeas. </i>Each of the Yozi possess a number of souls, the Demons of the Third Circle, who define and express their being. Each Demon of the Third Circle is in turn reflected in their souls, the less powerful the Demons of the Second Circle (who express facets of their <i>over-souls</i>). Demons of the First Circle are the least powerful kind of demon, <i>serfs </i>created by greater demons in order to perform specific functions. All demons from greatest to least are slaves, trapped in a land of eternal torment.<br /> <br /> Demons are not humans.<br /> <br /> Demons are alien beings. Most (not all) are sentient, sapient and at least as intelligent as the average human. But they do not think and behave as humans do. A demon might be driven into a killing frenzy by the sound of laughter, or be dependent on playing the harp to live as a human depends on breathing, be obsessed with abducting and swaddling babies. A demon isn\u2019t necessarily inherently <i>evil</i> as such, but they are inherently <i>different </i>to humans.<br /> <br /> That said, <i>most </i>demons possess at least some similarities to humans. They may not be <i>human </i>but they\u2019re still <i>people.</i> The Yozi that demons descend from are ancient, powerful and <i>broken</i> things: whilst each demon is an individual, no demon completely escapes this legacy.<br /> <br /> <u><b>What are demons for?</b></u><br /> <br /> Exalted is a role playing game. It\u2019s meant to be played by a group of people (dare I say, \u201cgroup of friends\u201d) for <i>enjoyment</i>. It is not a mathematical simulation of a world. It is not a solo exercise.<br /> <br /> Demons, like everything else in Exalted, are a <i>tool </i>designed to <i>help you have fun</i> by <i>telling an interesting story.</i><br /> <br /> If demons aren\u2019t helping you have fun, stop using them. The entire reason they exist is to help you have fun. Go have fun with something else instead.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Okay, but what can demons do?</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> Being people but not human, demons lend themselves to narratives about the morality of slavery, stories about nature vs nurture, tales about forgiveness, punishment and redemption, and building legends about right and wrong. All of these stories could be told with humans, of course, and they\u2019d be more powerful and harder hitting with humans.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s why people use demons instead.<br /> <br /> Just as Marvel Comics used fictional mutants with extraordinary powers to talk about racial issues, making a story more powerful and more moving does not always equate to being more fun. Hitting people where they live by reducing their daily struggles to a game for your entertainment can be\u2026 not fun.<br /> <br /> Not always. Sometimes people want to tell a narrative about the struggles they face. In which case, don\u2019t dress the story up with demons, give them humans who they can identify with and go to town. But if you don\u2019t want to treat these themes with a light touch, maybe push them to the background, then demons are your go-to.<br /> <br /> <u><b>I feel like you\u2019re just being obtuse at this point...</b></u><br /> <br /> Good. This is a primer on how to deal with demons after all\u2026<br /> <br /> <u><b>Why might <i>my character</i> summon demons?</b></u><br /> <br /> Why <i>wouldn\u2019t </i>they?<br /> <br /> Malfeas is a vast and sprawling land, larger even that Creation. Within it dwell demons hand-crafted to serve any manor of purpose that the Yozi and their souls can divine. Any task you might want to perform, there\u2019s a demon for that.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re playing one of the Exalted (and, let\u2019s face it, you <i>probably </i>are) then demons are mystically bound to serve your will.<br /> <br /> The question you should be asking is:<br /> <br /> <u><b>How do I have fun summoning demons?</b></u><br /> <br /> A good story starts at the beginning. A great story starts in the middle. Hold that thought, we\u2019ll return to the beginning in the middle.<br /> <br /> First go here and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xjPIOH8F8a0l74BdDF7Q23nCfZ-YX68Xr6JmmtznMw4/\" target=\"_blank\">read this</a>.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m just kidding, I know you\u2019ve already read that, and if you haven\u2019t read it before, you\u2019re not going to read it now. Let me sum up.<br /> <br /> Treantmonk surmises that there are archetypal \u201croles\u201d that get filled in role playing game groups (he also contests that blindly trying to fill these roles is a bad thing, but admits people do it anyway): The Fop (or party face) does the talking (not always, but when it\u2019s important); The Corpse (or rogue) sneaks ahead of the rest of the group, opening locked doors, disarming traps and running face first into monsters; The Gimp (or healbot) who\u2019s role is to \u201cservice\u201d the rest of the party between combats; and The Lump (or tank) who exists to beat down enemies in combat.<br /> <br /> Treantmonk then goes on to describe a fifth archetype: God (The Wizard), who controls the battlefield and the narrative, primarily through the use of minions that do god\u2019s bidding. Treantmonk enumerates six primary reasons why summoning minions is a good idea: they help you damage enemies, they help stop you being damaged by enemies, they can help control the conditions of the battlefield (slowing enemies down, and reducing their defenses), they help with your action economy, they can be used as mounts (making you faster, yes, but also giving access to mobility abilities like flight), they can see things you might not be able to see (such as invisible, immaterial spirits). And, from a purely stimulationist, mathematical point of view, all these things hold true in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Sounds fun doesn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Your poor wife!</b></u><br /> <br /> The problem, with god\u2019s approach to demon summoning, is that those <i>pesky other players </i>(including the Storyteller) who <i>also</i> want to have fun. Treantmonk talks about it in his guide, but the problem is <i><b>sooo </b></i>much worse in Exalted.<br /> <br /> The first lesson in demon summoning is simple: just because you <b>can </b>doesn\u2019t mean you <b>should</b>.<br /> <br /> Ask yourself two questions:<br /> 1) Is it fun?<br /> 2) Is it fun for everyone else?<br /> <br /> A lot of the time, one of those questions is going to come up \u201cno\u201d, and those times you <i>should not </i>summon demons. For many people, this can be a difficult lesson to learn. Too often RPGs condition players into a mindset of antagonism between the \u201cplayers\u201d and the \u201cdungeon master\u201d: The DM sets a puzzle that the players have to solve, and the players go all-out, using all their skills to solve it. Exalted really doesn\u2019t (at the default level) work like that. Exalted is about working together to <i>tell a story</i>. That story is going to involve solving puzzles and using skills, but Exalted is played at a level where the story can\u2019t survive open antagonism and outright competition between the players and the ST. All RPGs require suspension of disbelief, and all STs <i>can</i> beat the players: but STs generally <i>don\u2019t</i> beat the players. Getting into an arms race with the ST is going to create a weird, clunky quasi-story that\u2019s only barely supported by the accountant\u2019s wet dream (the 662 page Exalted rule book).<br /> <br /> <u><b>You said something about a beginning?</b></u><br /> <br /> Summoning a demon requires a six hour ritual, conducted with precise timing.<br /> <br /> In prior editions, said ritual needed to be tailored to the demon (or at least the type of demon) you are trying to summon and involved exotic ritual components and sigils.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a demanding feat whereby you draw a being from an eternal prison across the boundaries of reality, then break its will to yours. It requires ancient knowledge from a time before memory. It\u2019s fraught with the danger of unleashing (a small part of) hell on earth.<br /> <br /> And you wanted to reduce it to a dice roll, didn\u2019t you?<br /> <br /> Chances are, you\u2019re playing a Solar. A being in league with the Yozi. A demon clothed in human flesh set out to destroy the righteous. Anathema to the natural order of the world.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a pretty good reason why\u2026 well just about every NPC in existence doesn\u2019t want to let you conduct your precisely timed, mentally exacting ritual to bring another demon into the world.<br /> <br /> To have fun with demon summoning, I suggest, you know, actually playing out the summoning of the demon. Devote an entire session to it. Every time.<br /> <br /> Where are you doing it?<br /> Why are you doing it?<br /> How are you doing it?<br /> Who is trying to stop you?<br /> (And yes, we know &quot;when&quot; you're trying to do it -- but use the when to set the scene.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>And now for something completely different!</b></u><br /> <br /> And on that note, I suggest <i>not </i>actually playing out whatever you want to use the demon for. Read over the Skip It sidebar on page 212 and the Resolving Battles sidebar on page 205. Not every fight is worth playing out in full, and not every fight is going to end in death.<br /> <br /> If you summon a blood ape to go assassinate someone, then set a difficulty using page 185 and make one roll using the ape\u2019s grapple accuracy pool \u2013 if it succeeds, then the assassination works, if it fails then your blood ape is driven off, on a botch the blood ape is killed. Simples.<br /> <br /> If you have a blood ape bodyguard then narrate what that bodyguard does in combat without busting out the dice (or, alternatively, play using the blood ape and narrate what your Solar does). If the ST wants to win, then they\u2019re going to win. No matter how powerful your character is, the ST controls the gameworld: they can throw three \u201cyou but better\u201d characters at you whilst you\u2019re sleeping. So put aside thoughts as to whether having that bodyguard is \u201cworthwhile\u201d from a combat optimization point of view: you\u2019re already Exalted, you\u2019re in the top 1% of the gameworld power-wise. Consider if having a demonic bodyguard is <i>interesting</i> from a story point of view.<br /> <br /> Remember your blood ape bodyguard is a hulking, cat hating monster. A living, feral embassy of hell who lives to feast on blood and gore. It\u2019s not <a href=\"https://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0154.html\" target=\"_blank\">Vaarsuvius\u2019 Raven</a>. It\u2019s always there. Snarling, hungering, barely held in check by your indomitable will. It\u2019s not a power-up: it\u2019s a story hook. Lean into that.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Split the party</b></u><br /> <br /> Chances are you have five (or, more likely, fewer) mighty Solars in your Circle. To roam a land-mass larger than Earth\u2019s. Maybe you want to tell a story about how you save your tiny backwater village from the Realm, but Exalted lends itself to telling grand stories about the fates of nations: mighty heroes, roaming the world, fighting creatures of legend.<br /> <br /> Split up. You\u2019ll have more fun.<br /> <br /> But what do you do when your character is five thousand miles away?<br /> <br /> Play a demon.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Which demon should I summon?</b></u><br /> <br /> This is not always obvious.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition (2.0), neomah were <i>vastly</i> better combatants than erymanthoi. And they had a bunch of useful powers. And they didn\u2019t randomly murder cats. Third Edition is a lot better at making demons good at what they\u2019re supposed to be good at, but really look at their stat-lines and read the descriptions before making your choice.<br /> <br /> Remember that demons are characters in their own right. Treat them as such. Like <a href=\"https://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0674.html\" target=\"_blank\">Vaarsuvius\u2019 Raven</a>. And remember that whilst they might be people, they\u2019re not human. Find a demon that compliments the story <i>you want to tell </i>who also doesn\u2019t squick-out the entire table. I can\u2019t tell you which demons to summon, because I don\u2019t know your character and I don\u2019t know the players at your table.<br /> <br /> But you should have an open and honest discussion from the players at your table about what they expect from the game, and which themes (if any) make them uncomfortable. Play to that.<br /> <br /> Demons are incredibly versatile. If you\u2019re looking at Exalted\u2019s back catalog and/or homebrewing as you should, then there\u2019s a demon for every occasion. An agata might not be as good as Chariot of Aerial Conquest, and an erymanthus might not be as good as Supernal Melee Dawn, but you can have as many agata and erymanthoi and neomah and firim and sesseljae as you like for the low, low cost of 8 Solar XP. Like Lunar shape-shifting, demon summoning is crazy versatile.<br /> <br /> As an ST, you want to build a story around a summoner in a similar fashion to building one around Lunar shape-shifting. The labor intensive (and more rewarding way) is to give the players multiple paths to go down. If we have to rescue the princess from her tower, then let the PCs summon a couple of blood apes and attack the front gate, or let them summon a neomah to seduce the guards, or let them summon an agata to fly up to the top of the tower. Better yet, have a princess atop her tower, and put her sister on the battlefield fifty miles east, and have the players choose whom they\u2019re going to help in person, and whom is getting demons to come help them. The less labor intensive way is to simply raise the bar: the princess is a half-cat neko-girl so blood apes are a no go, the guards are eunuchs, and the tower is actually an underground dungeon \u2013 so demons can\u2019t actually help you. You\u2019re going to want to mix approaches, and encourage spot-light ceding.<br /> <br /> Fortunately demons aren\u2019t an insurmountable problem. Almost everyone in Creation is a mortal. And a blood ape can beat just about any mortal. A blood ape can\u2019t beat Ahlat. There\u2019s a lot of scope for making demon summoning useful, but not game defining. The demons are more powerful than 90% of the enemy opposition. The PCs are <i>vastly</i> more powerful than the demons.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Answers will I only chime, when questions put are asked in rhyme</b></u><br /> <br /> These are my first thoughts.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure many of you disagree.<br /> I\u2019m sure many more of you have read this far, and found that none of the advice I\u2019ve given you is useful.<br /> <br /> Good.<br /> <br /> Discuss:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-30-2020, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T16:05:21-07:00","id":1377404,"title":"","content":"I think summoning demons for combat and then not using them in combat deeply undermines their use. If I summoned 30 blood ape demon body guards as a battle group, I\u2019d assume I wanted them to do some fighting and some fighting with dice\u2014presumably that I the player would run, not the ST. This is extra so for the Second Circles. Now with things like single tasks, like the assassination example, I agree. Or crafting, or other parts where player interference doesn\u2019t matter and time isn\u2019t pressing. <br /> I think your approach to demons as primarily narrative elements is interesting even if I think demons actual talents and potential numbers are their value\u2014They provide logistics support and multiply the force for the party, which in 3e is vital. <br /> I\u2019m also...not sold on the idea that demons are there to explore slave morality stories, although I guess they could. That sort of narrative seems better suited for elementals, who have a chance at freedom\u2014while a demon you do not bind lives out an equally tyrannical if slightly more pleasant life in Malfeas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T02:11:32-07:00","id":1377479,"title":"","content":"Well, the thing is you summon demons to serve you; you create elementals, and they probably die after a month.<br /> <br /> Anyway. Some very good points John. Especially about making them part of the story.<br /> I do think that you should mention battlegroups though. And I think you talk too much about Christian demons, I'd more talk about Devas, Chinese and Japanese demons, etc.<br /> And I don't agree that splitting up means that you have more fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Our high-essence games tend to be split into 3 groups at once, which means you only play a third of a session. Getting PCs to play NPCs (like demons) is a good suggestion that we sometimes use, but doesn't always work. I'm now running a low-xp Lunars game where the PCs are mostly together, and it makes a big difference.<br /> <br /> Last, I think that you raise a good point about how first-circle demons are pretty weak compared to Exalts, but that doesn't necessarily apply to Second-Circles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T02:19:34-07:00","id":1377480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1377479#post1377479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the thing is you summon demons to serve you; you create elementals, and they probably die after a month.<br /> <br /> Anyway. Some very good points John. Especially about making them part of the story.<br /> I do think that you should mention battlegroups though. And I think you talk too much about Christian demons, I'd more talk about Devas, Chinese and Japanese demons, etc.<br /> And I don't agree that splitting up means that you have more fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Our high-essence games tend to be split into 3 groups at once, which means you only play a third of a session. Getting PCs to play NPCs (like demons) is a good suggestion that we sometimes use, but doesn't always work. I'm now running a low-xp Lunars game where the PCs are mostly together, and it makes a big difference.<br /> <br /> Last, I think that you raise a good point about how first-circle demons are pretty weak compared to Exalts, but that doesn't necessarily apply to Second-Circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elementals are a year and a day I believe? I\u2019m away from book at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T04:07:30-07:00","id":1377486,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the binding aspects of Summon Elemental, including its duration, now match that of Demon of the First Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T04:26:13-07:00","id":1377487,"title":"","content":"... although if the Wits+Occult roll fails a summoned elemental disperses back into raw elemental essence and the summoner merely does not regain expended willpower. <br /> <br /> Whereas failing to bind a summoned demon leaves the summoner to deal with an unbound and likely angry demon. Not an insignificant difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T10:24:24-07:00","id":1377531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1377487#post1377487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... although if the Wits+Occult roll fails a summoned elemental disperses back into raw elemental essence and the summoner merely does not regain expended willpower.<br /> <br /> Whereas failing to bind a summoned demon leaves the summoner to deal with an unbound and likely angry demon. Not an insignificant difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which hearkens back the wise old adage, &quot;Do not call up that which you can not put down.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T12:48:05-07:00","id":1378021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1377404#post1377404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think summoning demons for combat and then not using them in combat deeply undermines their use. If I summoned 30 blood ape demon body guards as a battle group, I\u2019d assume I wanted them to do some fighting and some fighting with dice\u2014presumably that I the player would run, not the ST. This is extra so for the Second Circles. Now with things like single tasks, like the assassination example, I agree. Or crafting, or other parts where player interference doesn\u2019t matter and time isn\u2019t pressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this approach is fun for you, then please enjoy it. If it's not fun for you, please consider my argument below:<br /> <br /> As an ST... &quot;eh&quot;:<br /> <br /> Let's say I come up with a story idea:<br /> <br /> The PCs get ambushed by wolves circling a dead body, let's say two wolves per PC for an even 10. The PCs defeat the wolves and find the body is animated by necromancy (albeit to badly mauled to move).<br /> <br /> The PCs venture into a nearby village and find it beset by hungry ghosts. The PCs dispatch the hungry ghosts, and treat with honored ancestor ghosts who reveal that a Deathknight has risen and is attacking villages.<br /> <br /> The PCs journey to attack the Deathknight, and have a grand fight with a Deathknight, Nephwrack, a size three battlegroup of zombies, a War Ghost and a Mortwright.<br /> <br /> Sounds reasonable to me.<br /> <br /> Only now the Twilight has thirty blood apes.<br /> <br /> What do I do with the wolves? Do I throw in a size 2 battlegroup of wolves and have a massive pack of 30-odd wolves randomly wandering Creation around a single dead body? Do I keep the original ten wolves and let the blood apes take them all out in a single turn of Principle of Motion Battlegroup Area Attacks?<br /> <br /> Do I really make the five solars fight hungry ghosts when the demons can fight them for them? Do I up the opposition so the blood apes have something different to fight?<br /> <br /> Do I make the boss fight more difficult?<br /> <br /> If I make fights more difficult, then what was the point of summoning the Blood Apes? And doesn't it make the story kinda ridiculous if the PCs are beset by enormous numbers of everything?<br /> <br /> Do I not make the fights more difficult and just let the blood apes roll over all opposition? And if the PCs are going to roll over all opposition, do we really have to bust out the dice and spend three hours rolling rather than just narrating that they win and moving on to the next thing?<br /> <br /> As a player... &quot;eeeeeeehhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh&quot;:<br /> <br /> I don't want to wait twice as long whilst you take two turns. Your demons are people in their own right who aren't psychically compelled to follow your exact instructions exactly as you narrate them. Where's my character going to sleep among your materialized bodyguards? Wyld Hunt much? I'm the Dawn, I want to be the focus for combat, not Octavian and his thirty blood apes!<br /> <br /> As someone who almost exclusively plays Twilights:<br /> <br /> Mwahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahah! UNLIMITED POWER!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T17:50:46-07:00","id":1378117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378021#post1378021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this approach is fun for you, then please enjoy it. If it's not fun for you, please consider my argument below:<br /> <br /> As an ST... &quot;eh&quot;:<br /> <br /> Let's say I come up with a story idea:<br /> <br /> The PCs get ambushed by wolves circling a dead body, let's say two wolves per PC for an even 10. The PCs defeat the wolves and find the body is animated by necromancy (albeit to badly mauled to move).<br /> <br /> The PCs venture into a nearby village and find it beset by hungry ghosts. The PCs dispatch the hungry ghosts, and treat with honored ancestor ghosts who reveal that a Deathknight has risen and is attacking villages.<br /> <br /> The PCs journey to attack the Deathknight, and have a grand fight with a Deathknight, Nephwrack, a size three battlegroup of zombies, a War Ghost and a Mortwright.<br /> <br /> Sounds reasonable to me.<br /> <br /> Only now the Twilight has thirty blood apes.<br /> <br /> What do I do with the wolves? Do I throw in a size 2 battlegroup of wolves and have a massive pack of 30-odd wolves randomly wandering Creation around a single dead body? Do I keep the original ten wolves and let the blood apes take them all out in a single turn of Principle of Motion Battlegroup Area Attacks?<br /> <br /> Do I really make the five solars fight hungry ghosts when the demons can fight them for them? Do I up the opposition so the blood apes have something different to fight?<br /> <br /> Do I make the boss fight more difficult?<br /> <br /> If I make fights more difficult, then what was the point of summoning the Blood Apes? And doesn't it make the story kinda ridiculous if the PCs are beset by enormous numbers of everything?<br /> <br /> Do I not make the fights more difficult and just let the blood apes roll over all opposition? And if the PCs are going to roll over all opposition, do we really have to bust out the dice and spend three hours rolling rather than just narrating that they win and moving on to the next thing?<br /> <br /> As a player... &quot;eeeeeeehhhhhhhhhhhhhhhh&quot;:<br /> <br /> I don't want to wait twice as long whilst you take two turns. Your demons are people in their own right who aren't psychically compelled to follow your exact instructions exactly as you narrate them. Where's my character going to sleep among your materialized bodyguards? Wyld Hunt much? I'm the Dawn, I want to be the focus for combat, not Octavian and his thirty blood apes!<br /> <br /> As someone who almost exclusively plays Twilights:<br /> <br /> Mwahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahahah! UNLIMITED POWER!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As an ST:<br /> Battle Groups can't use charms, per dev comment--so AOE attacks and Principle of Motion Attacks are homebrew already. That said.<br /> Fight 1: A battlegroup of wolves (becuase yes, 10 wolves should be a battle group) is a trivial fight. Yes. 1 round, Blood Apes, after wolves ambush. If your runnning them as individuals, for some reason, then run the fight. The BG will probably crash them, letting the party finish in 1-2 rounds. Might be a turn quicker than average, depending on the BG's iniative roll.<br /> Fight 2: Let the Battle group fight the battle group, Maybe up the size? Add a warghost? This fight also seems...trivially easy if you have a dawn. Reckon with the social effects of having a bunch of blood apes attakc. You mentioned this yourself in your first thing--the ancestor spirit might be frightened. <br /> Fight 3: a Size 2 Battle group on the Solars Size will make the fight easier but not trivial, but up the Zombies to something that isn't already non-threatening. THe Death Knight will make short work of a battlegroup if permitted, requiring the dawn. <br /> <br /> All 3 of these fights are too easy, depending on your party and exact essence numbers. Add in that the sorcerer is already plausibly going to anihilate the BG's with Obisidian butterflies every few turns and well. I am unimpressed.<br /> <br /> You both severely over and under estimate the power of a size 2 bg of blood apes. And if I've bound Octavian, at E3, and the Dawn feels shown up...the Dawn has done a bad job.<br /> <br /> For giving your blood ape orders, as an Eclipse ans Zenith Sorcerer: Get yourself a war charm or make a sorcerous commander or pick a blood ape as sargeant.<br /> <br /> As a player, if you make me treat each demon like more an individual than I would treat one of the soliders I bought with my command merit, I won't bother with demons. I have things to do, people to conquere, wyld hunts to attract. Wasting 3 hours of my day to summon 1 blood ape--to build a fortress or man a seige engine or whatever else I need done today--is wasting my time. Embrace that your an exalted sorcerer-. A solar or Dragonblooded or Lunar. These creatures and spirits <i>are </i> your servants, loyal to the point of dying for you. You, with time can bind hundreds to your will. If you have a player doing this, as an ST, then there should be consequences yes--enemies might bring mortal soliders, gods might take notice, frontal assualts become less likely. But there should be a chance for the player to enjoy the cathartic feeling of commanding his horde of blood apes to charge into the elite vanguard that's pinning the Dawn down, while the dawn fights the Five DB heroes.<br /> <br /> I'll note further, that slavery themes are exceptionally bad for demons. For the same reason their bad for X-men. The &quot;issue&quot; of slavery is grounded in the humanity of the other. Removing that humanity makes the ethical dilemna...silly. A firmin doesn't even have sapient thought, nor does a stomach bug. Nor are many of the creatures of malfeas human. Examining slavery without humanity is navel gazing--just as examining minoritiy rights like the X-men does, but without equalizing (the X-men <i>are</i> more dangerous than your average human, to the last).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T00:06:54-07:00","id":1378197,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11835_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11835\" data-vbnamecard=\"11835\">Epee102</a> Explain to me slowly, as if to a child.<br /> <br /> You want bound demons to be mechanically useful in a fight -- you want to roll dice with them.<br /> You also want me, as ST, to increase the difficulty of fights so your bound demons don't make the fights too easy.<br /> <br /> Aside from fights taking longer, what's the difference between that and just not summoning demons at all?<br /> <br /> Because the only difference I see is narrative -- you now have demons to use as a Story Hook.<br /> <br /> If the only difference is narrative, why am I taking twenty minutes out of my life to have you roll dice? (Especially as RAW, it's me, the ST who is supposed to be rolling the dice for NPC demons.)<br /> <br /> Can't the battlegroup of blood apes chew through the elite vanguard <i>in the background</i> whilst we focus on the real fight? You really want to make every blood ape you've summoned to man a seige engine roll dice? Really? Because that's your example, not mine...<br /> <br /> Is your (and your table's) enjoyment <i>really</i> enhanced by tracking your apes Willpower and Magnitude? I mean, if it is, great. Follow the general principles in Treantmonk's Wizard Guide. Have fun.<br /> <br /> (Sidenote: How do Blood Apes Materialize without Charms?)<br /> <br /> Of course I agree with you completely on the narrative concequences of summoning demons -- no frontal assaults, fightened ghosts, all that jazz is solid gold and the very reason to summon demons. I just don't agree that it's necessary or desirable to bust out dice to achieve those concequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-03-2020, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T00:25:56-07:00","id":1378199,"title":"","content":"Something wicked this way comes...<br /> <br /> Macbeth by way of Ray Bradbury","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T01:57:47-07:00","id":1378212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378197#post1378197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Sidenote: How do Blood Apes Materialize without Charms?)</div> </div> </div> </div>1st circle demons are naturally material. They wouldn't use their Dematerialize Charm while in a battlegroup.<br /> <br /> 2nd/3rd circle demons are naturally immaterial. But, since they are rarely battlegroups, but individuals with their own legend and narrative weight, they just use the Materialize Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T03:51:06-07:00","id":1378225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378197#post1378197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11835_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11835\" data-vbnamecard=\"11835\">Epee102</a> Explain to me slowly, as if to a child.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask and thou shalt recieve<br /> <br /> Your combats are already far too easy for a group of 5 Exalts, depending on how you run them. By which I mean: BG Size 1 of wolves is going to take one or 2 turns, letting the BG of Blood Apes shorten that to 1 is not a big deal. If it's 10 wolves, as invidiuals, then it might take 1-2 turns, depending on the charms the Dawn has--if this is E3(because you mention octavian), it will take 1 or 2 turns, at e1 it might take 3.<br /> <br /> If you can't split the difference between &quot;fight is trivial because of the battlegroup&quot; and &quot;fight is the same as if with the battlegroup&quot;...I don't know what to tell you, that's a long conversation. After all, a Battle group of Blood Apes is not that much more to run then a Battle Group of Tiger Warriors. I also don't...mind the fights being too easy. Again, 2/3 of your figths are already to <i>me</i> trivial encounters. I'd run them, because a quick and done fight can be fun, but...yeah, no, a BG of Blood Apes ain't showing up and dawn.<br /> <br /> Now to give you credit: If their &quot;offscreen&quot; they don't need to roll dice. If I have 3 seige engines, each manned by a team of 10 blood apes, no I don't need to roll <i>every</i> seige engine. Just the one near me I'm boosting with my dice. But if their on the battlefield with me, as my escort, then every dice roll they make <i>does</i> matter, because they effect every enemy in thier range band. <br /> <br /> and...your taking 20 minutes to roll BG dice? Get a dice roller man, c'mon. You roll 1 time for command, 1 time to hit, 1 time for damage. You don't even check charms! And as player, I only can command each turn, unless I've made a/summoned someone else to do the command.<br /> <br /> Now, on my end: What's the difference in effort and time between the blood ape army I've summoned and the command merits I've bought? Players can have battlegroups at their disposal, after all, and fairly easily. Is your solution &quot;you must send this asset, that the game gives mechancial weight to, that you can empower with your charms, off screen to make my challenge easier&quot;. <br /> <br /> My broader objection to your post , while combat is a specific example, is that you want to make demons have this great narrative weight--spend a session summoning each one, learn their names, give them personalities, give them social detriments--but you don't want to let players engage with them or use them mecahncially, with the rolls and stats they are given. Now, RAW, with Octavaian or the like sure, maybe then it's a bit more leg work to include another High Essence user in combat--I personally let players run their allies and BGs, unless the player is new. But I think going &quot;the point of this powerful and famous spell isn't the vast number of utility charms and dice it gives you, but the narrative you'd get with those things already&quot; is. Backwards to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T06:08:18-07:00","id":1378247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378212#post1378212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st circle demons are naturally material. </div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is right. Do you have a page reference?<br /> <br /> Blood Apes have the Materialize charm. Page 525.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-03-2020, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T06:32:09-07:00","id":1378250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378225#post1378225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ask and thou shalt recieve<br /> <br /> Your combats are already far too easy for a group of 5 Exalts, depending on how you run them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Needless to say, I disagree. But let's assume the fights are balanced to your liking before you add in 30 demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378225#post1378225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can't split the difference between &amp;quot;fight is trivial because of the battlegroup&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;fight is the same as if with the battlegroup&amp;quot;...I don't know what to tell you, that's a long conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to have it.<br /> <br /> Why are you having combat? What are you trying to achieve?<br /> <br /> And what's your goal here?<br /> <br /> My reading is that you want the fight to be made artificially harder, because you've summoned demons to make the fight easier, but you want a net effect of the fight being easier, and you want to control the NPCs (actually not unreasonable if your turn is command actions as you've indicated), and you're not content with simply removing an enemy battlegroup to fight off-screen because you want to roll dice?<br /> <br /> Is that a fair assessment, because I have an argument to address that but if I've misunderstood I don't want to be accused of a strawman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378225#post1378225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all, a Battle group of Blood Apes is not that much more to run then a Battle Group of Tiger Warriors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and would suggest running the Tiger Warriors offscreen too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378225#post1378225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if their on the battlefield with me, as my escort, then every dice roll they make <i>does</i> matter, because they effect every enemy in thier range band.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they're fighting a battlegroup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378225#post1378225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as player, I only can command each turn, unless I've made a/summoned someone else to do the command.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize I'm skirting bad-faith here, but you summoned 30 blood apes but couldn't find someone to command them for you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378225#post1378225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, on my end: What's the difference in effort and time between the blood ape army I've summoned and the command merits I've bought? Players can have battlegroups at their disposal, after all, and fairly easily. Is your solution &amp;quot;you must send this asset, that the game gives mechancial weight to, that you can empower with your charms, off screen to make my challenge easier&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many apologies, I thought this was clear:<br /> <br /> Yes. That is exactly my solution.<br /> <br /> Summoned demons, mortal armies, retainers/allies/familiars.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying &quot;never bust out the dice&quot;. But yeah, I'm certainly saying that not busting out the dice for your party NPCs is usually more fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378225#post1378225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My broader objection to your post , while combat is a specific example, is that you want to make demons have this great narrative weight--spend a session summoning each one, learn their names, give them personalities, give them social detriments--but you don't want to let players engage with them or use them mecahncially, with the rolls and stats they are given. Now, RAW, with Octavaian or the like sure, maybe then it's a bit more leg work to include another High Essence user in combat--I personally let players run their allies and BGs, unless the player is new. But I think going &amp;quot;the point of this powerful and famous spell isn't the vast number of utility charms and dice it gives you, but the narrative you'd get with those things already&amp;quot; is. Backwards to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you and your group enjoy the way you're playing, I am not encouraging you to change. But yes, that is the purpose of this guide: people do demon summoning &quot;forwards&quot; then come to this forum and complain they're not having any fun. So I suggest running them backward. I am perfectly happy to have this debate with you, because there will be people better served by your advice than mine.<br /> <br /> Have you ever made mechanical use of a zombie's &quot;Plaguebearer&quot; special attack? I haven't. Not once. But I've narrated effects for it. <br /> <br /> I really don't want to make blood apes roll to climb a crumbling wall at difficulty 2. Just let them climb the wall. I can see from the mechanical stats provided that they're good at climbing.<br /> <br /> The narrative isn't detached from the rolls and stats the demons are given. It's just about not giving them the same spotlight as the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T09:36:16-07:00","id":1378289,"title":"","content":"Huh. Must have been confusing them with elementals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T10:31:46-07:00","id":1378304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378250#post1378250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm willing to have it.<br /> <br /> Why are you having combat? What are you trying to achieve?<br /> <br /> And what's your goal here?<br /> <br /> My reading is that you want the fight to be made artificially harder, because you've summoned demons to make the fight easier, but you want a net effect of the fight being easier, and you want to control the NPCs (actually not unreasonable if your turn is command actions as you've indicated), and you're not content with simply removing an enemy battlegroup to fight off-screen because you want to roll dice?<br /> <br /> Is that a fair assessment, because I have an argument to address that but if I've misunderstood I don't want to be accused of a strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a few points of difference, before getting into this: If a fight would be resolved without rolling dice I don't usually have it in the docket. I just...don't run things like &quot;10 wolves jump 5 solars and get slaughtered.&quot; There's no clear narrative point to it. The hungry ghosts are closer, but that fight taking 2 turns seems...fine for it's narrative purpose.<br /> <br /> That first set of questions is very improtant however. I expect that if you, the ST, know I have 30 demons at my command, you would account for that either mechancially or narratively. Sometimes that means fights that were a bit difficult would be trivial. Sometimes it means swapping a Mortwright for another Abyssal, or the Abyssal spends a turn or two focusing on the BG, letting the Dawn get hits in better. Sometimes it means &quot;you parading 30 demons on the battlefield to end the fight quick got the ire of the local populace&quot;. It's very doable to make a BG feel impactful.<br /> <br /> So your assement is mostly correct, although I object to &quot;artificially harder&quot;. If summoning 30 blood apes makes the fight a simple win...let them have the simple win. Let them <i>roll</i> the simple win. Winning and showboating over weaker opponents can be fun! Especially if the combat is narratively important! To crib from my own game, there was a fight where 5 blood apes took on two solars, a giant lion, a dragonblooded, and a fae-touched human. The blood Apes got slaughtered in 2 turns, and only barely landed one punch--but it was fun! Because the players got to be awesome! Let the Twlight's battlegroup oblierate the enemies--the Abyssals gonna go through them like mincemeat anyway, and the Dawn's almost certaintly still going to be the show off in a fight!<br /> <br /> I had another combat where the party lead 2 BGs (different cities millitias with diferent training) to ambush an enemy army. It was a two turn route, and they massacred the miniboss--but it was rewarding to see the dice play out the plan they made. The math rocks make it feel real!<br /> <br /> As to your question about removing an enemy battlegroup:<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378250#post1378250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless they're fighting a battlegroup.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not RAW, by the by. It depends on the size of the BG, so maybe the horde of zombies would soak it up, but its is far from universal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378250#post1378250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize I'm skirting bad-faith here, but you summoned 30 blood apes but couldn't find someone to command them for you?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A fair comment. When my players have a BG, they usually have a sargeant or commander character that rolls and acts on the same turn. My point was more &quot;Players will directly command only 1 BG when they give direct commands, with that entire abillity dedicated to giving armies commands&quot;. You could run the BG with the sargeant. My point was &quot;if your worried about the players having too many actions or taking too long&quot;.<br /> <br /> All in all, I've seen 1 post about someoen complaining about demons. It was a post I skimmed, so I don't know the whole context. And if your party enjoys your style, you do you. I spent the majority of this picking bones at what to me look like a waste of mechnaical tools and write ups. If I was playing an abyssal, I'd expect to roll my zombie hordes actions instead of just run them by fiat--fiat feels arbitrary in a way that dice does not (It's an illsuion, sure, but the more fiat comes in, the more it feels like an improv game instead of an RPG. I have this big crunchy book I love, telling me to <i>not</i> use it seems...weird).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1103_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1103\" data-vbnamecard=\"1103\">Tikor</a>, yeah your thinking of elementals. The answer to &quot;how do they form BGs if they can't use charms&quot; is either: THey can use charms when deliberately ordered to or Materialize and Hurry Home are exceptions, since their entirely movement/utility charms. I generally allow BGs to use some if not all theirexisting charms.<br /> <br /> My only point of contention with your post that is past &quot;taste&quot; is...yeah, seriously, don't use demons to examine themes of slavery. Don't use elementals either. Its a conversation to have, I suppose, but demons and elementals are often too far removed from human to make it relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 04-03-2020, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T10:56:20-07:00","id":1378308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378304#post1378304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not RAW, by the by. It depends on the size of the BG, so maybe the horde of zombies would soak it up, but its is far from universal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 208:<br /> <br /> &quot;Area Attacks: Like other characters, battle groups can only make a single attack on their turn, but these are often large attacks, consisting of hundreds of flashing blades or sheets of arrows darkening the sky. As a result, when a battle group makes a close-ranged attack, it makes a single attack roll and applies that roll\u2019s results to all enemies in direct contact with the group (depending on the battle group\u2019s Size, this could potentially cover a considerable area). When a battle group makes a ranged attack, it must select a single primary target for the attack. If this target is another battle group, the attack resolves normally; if it\u2019s an individual, then the attack is also applied to all other individual characters (friendly or hostile) within close range of that target.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your battlegroup can only target a single battlegroup with ranged attacks, and only characters embattled with it in melee. (If you embattle another battlegroup upto a size larger than you, they can't move.)<br /> <br /> It's not universal but it's pretty close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-03-2020, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T12:29:25-07:00","id":1378318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378250#post1378250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summoned demons, mortal armies, retainers/allies/familiars.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying &quot;never bust out the dice&quot;. But yeah, I'm certainly saying that not busting out the dice for your party NPCs is usually more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with John on this one. As a player I can take a retainer captain-general of my army, who uses his own merit dots to get the actual army and the resources to support it. I can also grab a Tyrant Lizard familiar, and a few more young dragonblooded bodyguards. So then when I'm rolling into battle you've got me, my captain-general, my two bodyguards, my T-rex, my battlegroup of soldiers and my captain's bodyguards as well. Then the Twilight asks to roll in himself, his battlegroup of bloodapes, his Tomescue bodyguard, his special assassin made by the Ephemeral Induction Technique, and Octavian, who's he's just learned to summon.<br /> <br /> At some point you have to go &quot;Okay, guys, I know you bought all those merits, and you should be able to use them, but this is making combat a nightmare, and it's making the whole campaign terribly unwieldy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> What I try to do now is actually take a leaf out of the RPG Star Trek: Adventues. In that you have main characters, who are basically the PCs, but also a host of supporting characters. Who are nebulously NPCs, except in cases where one PC is off without the other PCs somewhere. So for example if your first officer is planetside with two supporting characters, then the players take control of them. It can even be the case where only supporting cast members go and do something, and the players just transition there.<br /> <br /> So if I've got a circle of players with like 10-15 various powerful familiars, battlegroups, retainers, etc. We have a bit of an agreement that they're not just going to bring them everywhere. For one it's almost totally pointless if they're powerful Solars, since adding those factors is just going to make them win harder, in a lot of cases anyway. What it's better to do with them instead is to make them go places so the PCs can have influence in more than one place, which can either be onscreen with the players taking command of the NPCs or just offscreen success/failure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That way players still change the game with their merits, just like how they can change the game with their spells or their charms or their actions. You get to really feel your character as a military commander sending forces off to do one thing or another, while maybe keeping one battlegroup with yourself at all times, but it doesn't become awful for me to run as an ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T13:33:23-07:00","id":1378329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378318#post1378318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I try to do now is actually take a leaf out of the RPG Star Trek: Adventues. In that you have main characters, who are basically the PCs, but also a host of supporting characters. Who are nebulously NPCs, except in cases where one PC is off without the other PCs somewhere. So for example if your first officer is planetside with two supporting characters, then the players take control of them. It can even be the case where only supporting cast members go and do something, and the players just transition there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea a lot. I was thinking it would be cool to have a game where it logically makes sense to have a big supporting cast allied with the players - following Star Trek, it could be travel-in-a-ship-based, or it could be military- or government-themed. Then you could get the players to build that cast with their Merits and in-game abilities, hopefully giving them more ownership and investment in them. The players and ST could even work together to make a list of useful supporting roles, like medic, spy, or something, and make sure they have them all filled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if I've got a circle of players with like 10-15 various powerful familiars, battlegroups, retainers, etc. </div> </div> </div>I was thinking you could even use Allies for this if you really aren't going to use them very often. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have a bit of an agreement that they're not just going to bring them everywhere. For one it's almost totally pointless if they're powerful Solars, since adding those factors is just going to make them win harder, in a lot of cases anyway. What it's better to do with them instead is to make them go places so the PCs can have influence in more than one place, which can either be onscreen with the players taking command of the NPCs or just offscreen success/failure.<br /> <br /> That way players still change the game with their merits, just like how they can change the game with their spells or their charms or their actions. You get to really feel your character as a military commander sending forces off to do one thing or another, while maybe keeping one battlegroup with yourself at all times, but it doesn't become awful for me to run as an ST. </div> </div> </div>Thinking about action in two different places at once, instead of the Star Trek-y model where people offscreen are assumed to be doing pretty boring stuff, is harder for me, but it's definitely something I should try to incorporate more into my own game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T13:57:37-07:00","id":1378340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378329#post1378329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about action in two different places at once, instead of the Star Trek-y model where people offscreen are assumed to be doing pretty boring stuff, is harder for me, but it's definitely something I should try to incorporate more into my own game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah if you're going to do that basically just be like &quot;The PCs want to bring this guy in for questioning, but they're doing important things in the capital, so they're sending their guys off to go get him, I'll decide right now that with what they've sent, and unbeknownst to the players he's secretly a Lunar, that he'll give their forces the slip, but they will catch his personal assistant, who knows too much.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then don't even worry about it for a bit until it makes sense that enough time has passed that they show back up and it's dramatically appropriate to do so.*<br /> <br /> Or make some other problems in the city, like for example civil unrest during an epidemic and people flooding the streets, so they send their size 5 battlegroup of elite soldiers to keep everyone in their houses, maybe watched over by some of the PC's allies/retainers to make sure they aren't going too far and being brutes about it. That way the streets being patrolled by elite soldiers becomes more of a change of backdrop, rather than imagining exactly what's happening everywhere at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> *EDIT: Maybe make an actual note of it, but your players will probably end up reminding you at some point anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 04-03-2020, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T15:23:52-07:00","id":1378369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378340#post1378340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah if you're going to do that basically just be like &quot;The PCs want to bring this guy in for questioning, but they're doing important things in the capital, so they're sending their guys off to go get him, I'll decide right now that with what they've sent, and unbeknownst to the players he's secretly a Lunar, that he'll give their forces the slip, but they will catch his personal assistant, who knows too much.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then don't even worry about it for a bit until it makes sense that enough time has passed that they show back up and it's dramatically appropriate to do so.*<br /> <br /> Or make some other problems in the city, like for example civil unrest during an epidemic and people flooding the streets, so they send their size 5 battlegroup of elite soldiers to keep everyone in their houses, maybe watched over by some of the PC's allies/retainers to make sure they aren't going too far and being brutes about it. That way the streets being patrolled by elite soldiers becomes more of a change of backdrop, rather than imagining exactly what's happening everywhere at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> *EDIT: Maybe make an actual note of it, but your players will probably end up reminding you at some point anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! <br /> <br /> I'm playing right now, but I will probably end up STing at some point in the future. I was thinking about it from a player's perspective, so thinking about what are the problems our ST has currently told us about in the satrapy we liberated from the realm and which ones we should send our allies to (attempt to) deal with. But I should probably think about it also for my future campaign...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T16:05:42-07:00","id":1378389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378369#post1378369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks!<br /> <br /> I'm playing right now, but I will probably end up STing at some point in the future. I was thinking about it from a player's perspective, so thinking about what are the problems our ST has currently told us about in the satrapy we liberated from the realm and which ones we should send our allies to (attempt to) deal with. But I should probably think about it also for my future campaign...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to be thinking about this from the ST side of things, it does also free you up to giving the characters lots of reasons to use their allies. Like maybe there's something that needs investigating in several areas, and it's time sensitive or something. It's normally something that, as a gamemaster, you need to shy away from because splitting the party sucks, but if they have enough allies you can just forget about it and throw like three things at them at once, or throw boring but possibly important side tasks and the like.<br /> <br /> Like for example if your Solar healer has a little cadre of physicians who follow her around and learn from her, you can have them treat a bunch of people at once while the Solar goes after the people who are minutes away from death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T14:29:29-07:00","id":1378617,"title":"","content":"Edit: Wrong thread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-04-2020, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T15:15:46-07:00","id":1378621,"title":"","content":"If anyone intends to use this advise as stated, I'd recommend that you be very upfront with your players about it. If I went through an entire session summoning a demonic bodyguard and then afterwards I was told that I had to pick between having my bodyguard and my Solar with ~3 combat charms take part in combat, I'd (metaphorically) flip the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","user":"Speedbump","date":".  thought it, didn't write it 04-04-2020, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T15:59:13-07:00","id":1378624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Speedbump</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377395-by-the-pricking-of-my-thumbs-\u2013-john-doe\u2019s-guide-to-demon-summoning-3e?p=1378621#post1378621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anyone intends to use this advise as stated, I'd recommend that you be very upfront with your players about it. If I went through an entire session summoning a demonic bodyguard and then afterwards I was told that I had to pick between having my bodyguard and my Solar with ~3 combat charms take part in combat, I'd (metaphorically) flip the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s why I told my players up front for the DB game, no more Young Dragonblooded retainers than PCs, so in this case five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-22T13:37:47-08:00","id":1547897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div c